      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “treatment bias” as “prejudice or skewed judgment in care”; it refers to “stigmatising attitudes” and the need to “limit treatment bias,” but the specific wording about prejudice/skewed judgment is not directly supported.",
        "While the packet supports that providers’ attitudes/beliefs (including perceptions of people who use drugs as dangerous, blameworthy, and incapable of recovery) relate to “treatment bias” and that addressing these attitudes can foster better relationships, the definition’s first sentence includes an additional characterization (“prejudice or skewed judgment”) that is not stated in the packet."
